distance_hb_zero_point,dataset,*,g_obs,given,0.049,,,mag,,as_released,gc_distance_hb,distance_hb_slope,not_published,"Harris 1996, AJ 112, 1487, 2010 edition (arXiv 1012.3224v1)",l. 148,"Harris does not say what its ± means. R_Sun and L_V move together, so g_bar is unchanged (F1). Correlated with distance_hb_slope (one fit; correlation not published). The calibration includes dynamical parallaxes (l. 125–127); D-036 #6 is not triggered (D-099 rule 3)",
